# SmolVLM EAGLE-3: H_full @ layer 0 vs 1-layer baseline

Both run **exactly one draft layer**, isolating draft-step cost against acceptance quality.

- 80 prompts, `OUTPUT_LEN=1024`, `max_num_seqs=1`, `num_spec_tokens=4`, eager
- H_full: `~/tmp/bridge_ablation/H_full/checkpoint-66466` + `EAGLE3_FORCE_EXIT_LAYER=0`
- M1: `output/smolvlm_256m_eagle3_nccl/checkpoint-66466`

Speedup is **ms per output token**, not wall time: at temp 1 the runs sample different
text and stop at different lengths, so wall time compares unequal work. ms/token is
equivalent to truncating both to the same token count.

